meta {
  name: Character read
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/characters/{{playerName}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  ## Character read

  Read a character by name, online or offline.

  - Method and path: `GET /api/v1/characters/{{playerName}}`. Replace `{{playerName}}` with any
    character name.
  - Path parameters: `name` — character name, case-insensitive, letters and digits only (max 24).
    A name that fails this pattern returns `404 not_found`.
  - Query parameters: none.
  - Body: none.
  - Signature headers: `X-GM-Timestamp`, `X-GM-Nonce`, `X-GM-Signature`, set by `collection.bru`.
    No `X-GM-Actor`, no RBAC permission.
  - Success: `200` with `{"guid","name","account_id","account_name","level","race","class","online"}`.
    `guid` is a 64-bit value; above 2^53 it loses precision in JavaScript clients.
  - Failure: `401 unauthorized`, `404 target_not_found` when the character does not exist,
    `405 method_not_allowed`, `409 replayed_nonce`, `429 rate_limited`, `503 world_unavailable`.

  The read uses the character cache on the world thread; a stalled world thread returns `503`.
}
